<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa unions to bid for Protea - report.</title>
<headline>S.Africa unions to bid for Protea - report.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Congress of South African Trade Unions (Cosatu) has put together a consortium with other black groups to bid for control of insurance firm Protea Assurance Co Ltd from Britain's Royal Sun Alliance, Business Day said on Monday.</p>
<p>Union sources said a bid price of 100 rand a share had been submitted to Protea's adviser, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell. Protea shares closed on Friday at 91.50.</p>
<p>The paper said other parties to have tendered for Protea included South African Eagle Insurance Co Ltd, Guardian and National, Board of Executors, Mutual and Federal and Commercial Union of South Africa.</p>
<p>The final outcome of the bidding is expected to be announced by the end of the month.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
